\caption(Annual passenger totals and calendar exposure, with monthly totals and daily averages plotted separately. The scales have different units; the right-hand plot is not daily-resolution data.)
\alttext(Two time-series panels showing increasing airline passenger totals and their calendar-day averages from 1949 to 1960. Both retain strong seasonal swings.)

Calendar length explains part of the difference between months. To show
its size, group all Januaries, Februaries and so on over the twelve years.
A 28-day February needs fewer passengers than a 31-day January to have the
same daily average. Group means remain descriptive: the dataset has trend
and seasonality, not randomly assigned month lengths.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/zeller_monthly_profile.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto air = dm::algorithms::gregorian_month_features(dm::datasets::air_passengers()) |
      dm::mutate("daily", [](const auto& r) { return r.get_double("passengers") / r.get_double("calendar_days"); });
  const auto profile = air | dm::group_by("month") | dm::summarise(
      dm::agg::mean("passengers", "mean_monthly_total"), dm::agg::mean("calendar_days", "mean_days"),
      dm::agg::mean("daily", "mean_daily_average"));
  std::print("{}\n", profile.to_md(5));
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
      .line(profile.get_column("month").values(), profile.get_column("mean_daily_average").values(),
            "calendar-day average", dm::RGB{37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .points(profile.get_column("month").values(), profile.get_column("mean_daily_average").values(), "", dm::RGB{37, 99, 235}, 4)
      .title("Seasonality remains after calendar normalisation")
      .x_label("month (1=January)").y_label("mean thousands per calendar day")
      .size(900, 460).save_svg("build/zeller_monthly_profile.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| month | mean_monthly_total | mean_days | mean_daily_average |
